# What does not belong in the build context.
#
# The API's Dockerfile copies named paths rather than `COPY . .`, so nothing
# here is load-bearing for what ends up in the image. It is here for two other
# reasons: the context is uploaded to the builder on every build, and `.env` is
# the one file in this repository that must never leave the machine it is on.

.git
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. The image builds its own; a stale local dist must never win.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.expo
**/.expo
coverage
**/coverage

# Secrets. `.env.example` is the template and is committed; `.env` is real.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Nothing here is needed to build or run the server.
*.log
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# NOT excluded, deliberately: docs/theory and docs/legal.
#
# The API reads both from disk at runtime — the assistant's system prompt comes
# from the corpus so it cannot drift from the document, and the BAA's
# frontmatter is the only source of the version anyone accepts. Excluding
# `docs/` here would break the image in a way that only shows up when the
# assistant is switched on, or when a clinician tries to accept the agreement.
